            <ArticleTitle>[A girl with abdominal pain and haematomas on the belly].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>D1149</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 14-year-old girl with anorexia nervosa was referred to our paediatric hospital. She had a five-day history of severe abdominal pain. On abdominal sonography and MRI a duodenal wall hematoma was seen, correlating anatomically to abdominal bruises found on physical examination. The girl admitted to self-injury related to her eating disorder.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
